# =============================================================================
# mul-mean — S3-B1 non-exact Mul+Mean device fixture (gpu-training-lowering)
# =============================================================================
#
# What this is: the differentiable device workload `loss = mean(x · w)` over
# N = 1000 elements — a device-resident forward kernel (elementwise mul +
# tree-reduction mean) with the AIR-generated backward companion
# `loss_backward` (scalar 1/N division, fill/broadcast, elementwise gradient
# accumulation, (grad_x, grad_w) tuple outputs). This is the shape precedent
# admitted to the AIR lane by the SEM059 relaxation (@ nucleum + @ radix
# lane "air" + @ radix backward).
#
# This file is READ-ONLY: it is the pinned oracle input (S2-5 convention).
# The host input values live in faber.toml `[device] inputs`; the CPU
# reference is pinned in oracle/ under numeric-policy v1.0.0 gradient row
# (atol = rtol = 1e-4; FD central eps = 1e-3, numeric-policy §4).
#
# Honesty gate (C3, stage-3-delivery.md N3.7): inputs are NON-half-integer /
# NON-structurally-exact. N = 1000 (not a power of two) and
# x[i] = (10·(i+1)+3)/100, w[i] = (10·(i+1)+7)/100. The analytic gradients
# x[i]/N and w[i]/N reduce to fractions whose denominator keeps a factor
# 5^4/5^5 (numerators ≡ 3 / 7 mod 5, never divisible by 5), so NO gradient
# element is exactly representable in f32 — the device's f32 results round
# and the 1e-4 floor is exercised with honest non-zero deltas, never the
# S0-D delta-0 backstop. oracle/tools/honesty_check.py proves this and
# REJECTS structurally-exact alternatives (oracle/tools/exact-alt.fab).
#
# See also: gradus/exempla/gradient-seam (shape precedent),
# examples/training/device-summa-recollige (S2-5 fixture convention),
# stage-3-delivery.md §4 S3-B1.
# =============================================================================

# nil() — vacuum residual for the companion backward ABI.
functio nil() → vacuum {
    tacet
}

@ nucleum
@ radix lane "air"
@ radix backward "loss_backward"
functio simple_loss(tf32[1000] x, tf32[1000] w) → f32 {
    fixum tensor<f32, [1000]> product ← x.multiply(w)
    redde product.mean()
}
